SF0042S3002/FAILED
Page 2-lines 16 and 17 Delete entirely and insert:

"(ii) Include a full-service restaurant that shall be open for
business for not less than twelve (12) hours each day and for not less than six
(6) days each week. At the discretion of the appropriate licensing authority,
variances to this time requirement may be granted on a seasonal basis. As used
in this paragraph, "full-service restaurant" means a restaurant where waiters
deliver food and drink offered from a printed food menu to patrons at tables or
booths and a restaurant that has a dining room or rooms, kitchen and the number
and kind of employees necessary for the preparing, cooking and serving of meals.
For purposes of this paragraph, the service of only fry orders or sandwiches,
hamburgers or salads shall not qualify as a full-service restaurant;". GIERAU
